---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="About - Manuel Gil - Software Developer & Open Source Maintainer"
  description="Software developer who builds and carries open source tools — VSCode extensions, libraries, and utilities."
  keywords="manuel gil, software developer, open source maintainer, vscode extensions, json flow, developer tools, typescript, angular, vue.js"
>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 pt-20">
    <section class="flex items-center justify-center py-32">
      <div class="max-w-3xl text-center">
        <h1
          class="mb-4 bg-linear-to-r from-primary to-accent bg-clip-text text-6xl font-bold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-transparent"
        >
          About Me
        </h1>
        <p class="mb-8 text-xl text-zinc-400">
          I'm Manuel Gil, a software developer. I build and carry open source tools —
          mostly <strong class="text-zinc-200">VSCode extensions</strong>,
          <strong class="text-zinc-200">npm packages</strong>, and small utilities.
          I work with <strong class="text-zinc-200">TypeScript, Angular, NestJS, VueJS, and PHP</strong>.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-8 text-xl text-zinc-400">
          I started self-taught. I still work mostly alone. Some of the things I've built
          have been downloaded and used more than I expected. I remain responsible for what I publish,
          but I don't promise availability or support.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto mb-32 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold">What I Actually Do</h2>
        <ul class="mb-6 space-y-4 text-zinc-400">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">Carry existing tools:</strong> A real part of what I do is
            keeping things working where I can — updating dependencies, fixing bugs,
            ensuring compatibility. Not all projects get the same attention or pace.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">Build new things when needed:</strong> I still create
            new tools, but only when there's a real gap. VSCode extensions, npm packages,
            browser utilities — whatever the problem asks for.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">Talk about it sometimes:</strong> I've spoken at
            events and meetups about open source and the tools I carry. I do this when I have
            something honest to say, not to build an audience.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">Use AI and messy workflows:</strong> I use whatever
            helps me get the work done — AI, forks, rough prototypes. But I review everything
            that ships. I'm responsible for what gets published.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <div class="mt-12 grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2">
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-bold text-primary">What I Work With</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-zinc-400">
              <li class="flex items-center">
                <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
                TypeScript, Angular, VueJS
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center">
                <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
                NestJS, PHP
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center">
                <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
                VSCode extension development
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center">
                <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
                npm packages and CLI tools
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-bold text-primary">Limits</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-zinc-400">
              <li class="flex items-center">
                <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
                I work alone on most of this
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center">
                <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
                My time is limited — response is not guaranteed
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center">
                <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
                Some projects are more active than others
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center">
                <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
                I prioritize stability over new features
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
